.TH MDS-FIND 8 "2026" "Lattice" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mds\-find \- search the Lattice metadata catalogue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mds\-find
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ predicates ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mds\-find
searches the pnfs\-mds catalogue for entries matching attribute
predicates, querying the metadata backend directly rather than walking
the namespace over NFS.  A search costs one backend table scan instead of
the millions of NFSv4 round trips a client\-side walk would need.
.PP
Attribute predicates are pushed to the backend data nodes, so
non\-matching rows are discarded before they cross the wire.  Name
matching is completed locally with
.BR fnmatch (3),
so
.B \-name
behaves exactly as it does in
.BR find (1).
.PP
The tool is strictly read\-only; it never mutates the catalogue.
.SH PREDICATES
All predicates are optional and are combined with logical AND.
.TP
.BI \-type " f|d|l|b|c|p|s"
File type: regular, directory, symlink, block device, character device,
FIFO, or socket.
.TP
.BI \-size " +N|-N"
Size larger than
.RI ( + )
or smaller than
.RI ( \- )
N bytes.  N accepts a
.BR K ,
.BR M ,
.BR G ,
.BR T ,
or
.B P
suffix (binary multiples).
.TP
.BI \-mtime " +N|-N"
Modified more than N days ago
.RI ( + ),
or within the last N days
.RI ( \- ).
.TP
.BI \-ctime " +N|-N"
Changed more than N days ago, or within the last N days.
.TP
.BI \-uid " N"
Owner uid.
.TP
.BI \-gid " N"
Owner gid.
.TP
.BI \-name " GLOB"
Entry\-name glob.  Supports
.BR * ,
.BR ? ,
and
.B [...]
character classes.
.TP
.BI \-inum " N[-M]"
Exact fileid, or an inclusive fileid range.  An exact fileid is served by
a single keyed read rather than a scan.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to mds.conf (default
.IR /etc/pnfs\-mds/mds.conf ).
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Maximum number of results, 1..10000000 (default 10000).  The scan stops
as soon as the limit is reached.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit one JSON object per match instead of the table format.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
One line per match:
.IP
type+mode nlink uid gid size mtime fileid name
.PP
Results are reported in backend scan order, which is not stable between
runs.  Each result carries the entry name, not a full path; an entry
whose name cannot be resolved is shown as
.BR ? .
.SH EXAMPLES
Regular files larger than 1 GiB named *.parquet:
.IP
.B mds\-find \-type f \-size +1G \-name '*.parquet'
.PP
Files modified in the last seven days:
.IP
.B mds\-find \-type f \-mtime \-7
.PP
Stale files owned by uid 1000, capped at 500 results:
.IP
.B mds\-find \-uid 1000 \-mtime +90 \-\-limit 500
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success (including a search with no matches), and 1 on
invalid arguments, configuration failure, or a backend error.
.SH PERFORMANCE
Each query scans every fragment of the inode table, so the work competes
with the NFS hot path for backend CPU.  Keep broad queries bounded with
.BR \-\-limit ,
and prefer running large searches from an admin node.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mds\-admin (8),
.BR mds.conf (5),
.BR find (1),
.BR fnmatch (3)
.PP
For the HTTP query service and the client\-side wrapper, see
.I docs/find\-api.md
in the Lattice distribution.
